          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score more points than opponents by winning hand comparisons and earning royalties. Avoid fouling (Back < Middle or Middle < Front).',
          gameplay: '1. **Initial deal**: 5 cards each, set face-up into the three hands. 2. **Draw phase**: Clockwise, each player draws 1 card, exposes it, and places it in one hand. 3. **Repeat** until all 13 cards are set. 4. **Showdown**: Compare Back vs Back, Middle vs Middle, Front vs Front against each opponent. 5. **Foul**: If Back < Middle or Middle < Front, you score 0 and pay 6 pts per opponent. 6. **Scoring**: 1 pt per hand won; 3 pt scoop bonus; royalties for straights, flushes, full houses, etc. 7. **Fantasyland**: QQ+ in Front (without fouling) gives 13 cards dealt at once on the next hand.',
          keyRules: [
            'Back (5) must be â‰¥ Middle (5) â‰¥ Front (3) in strength.',
            'Front hand: only pairs/trips/high card (no straights or flushes).',
            'Foul = 0 score, pay 6 pts per opponent.',
            '1 pt per hand won; 3 pt sweep bonus; royalties vary by position.',
            'Fantasyland: QQ+ in Front â†’ next hand get 13 cards at once.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Don't foul. Build a strong bottom hand early. Front hand: pairs or trips only.",
          intermediate: 'Push for Fantasyland: QQ in Front is worth the foul risk. Track opponent cards to know dead outs.',
          advanced: 'Outs calculation: if 8 spades are visible and you need one for a flush, switch to safe setting. Monte Carlo for hand-strength simulation.',
          tips: [
            'Pairs belong in Middle unless Bottom is already set or better.',
            'In Fantasyland, prioritise staying in (Trips Front, Quads Back).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
